LIVI change for the cluster's round centre panel (github.com/f-io/LIVI, dev branch at b43c7153): a setting
customHideNav. While the custom page is in front and the setting is on, the navigation rail (with its clock) is
not drawn at all and the custom page gets the whole window, so clusterd's round speedometer and settings page
fill the circle. Off by default: LIVI behaves exactly as before. Apply with `git apply`, then regenerate the
TypeScript contract (LIVI_WRITE_CONTRACT=1 cargo test -p livi-core-proto typescript_contract_is_current),
rebuild livi-core and the UI (pnpm run build:app). Written so it can be offered upstream.

